// ============================================================================
//  mod_wavegun_swell.zone  -  THE BODY SWELL OF MOON'S WAVE GUN  (v2.15.45)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This is the material half of the microwave sizzle death. The script half is
//  in scripts/zm/zapgun.gsc (server: raises Moon's expand clientfield on the
//  "expand" notetrack) and scripts/zm/zapgun.csc (client: Moon's
//  microwavegun_bloat(), which maps shader constant 0 to "scriptVector3" and
//  ramps its W from 0 to 0.5 over 2500 ms).
//
//  WHY MATERIALS. Moon's own zombie materials carry a MaximumSwell constant
//  (literal 20,0,0,1); it is kept for parity with Moon's material authoring
//  (the shader reads scriptVector3, the material constant is not consulted). MEASURED
//  2026-09-12, this job: the DLC5 techsets
//  mc_sw4_3d_char_cloth_4z8fq5wu_dlc5 / mc_sw4_3d_char_skin_j92387z3_dlc5
//  dump byte-identical to the retail techsets mc_sw4_3d_char_cloth_4z8fq5wu /
//  mc_sw4_3d_char_skin_j92387z3 already in mod.ff - every technique name is
//  the same pimp_technique_sw4_3d_char_* - so the swell vertex shader is
//  RETAIL. The only missing pieces were the material constant and the ramp.
//
//  WHAT SHIPS: 53 stock zombie body/head materials re-authored with
//  MaximumSwell added, dumped from the maps' own zones and otherwise
//  byte-for-byte what those zones already contained:
//    so_zclassic_zm_transit.ff  31  (zombie1/2/3 bodies, heads k/l/n/a)
//    zm_highrise.ff             14  (civ shorts, soldier, scientist, leaper,
//                                    chinese heads, commander helmet)
//    zm_prison.ff               17  (guard, inmate parts, vtn nva1, Brutus
//                                    body/gloves/head/helmet, mask heads,
//                                    barbwire/hellcatraz/slackjaw heads)
//    zm_nuked.ff                11  (hazmat bodies 1/2, heads 1-4 + mask,
//                                    soldier/solciv bodies)  [counted below]
//  Player-character materials are deliberately NOT included: the client ramp
//  only ever runs for actors that get the clientfield, and keeping it that way
//  means a hit player can never deform.
//
//  NUKETOWN'S 25 IMAGES. zm_nuked.ff is not one of build_ff.bat's --load
//  inputs (its zombie set reaches no other map), so the image dependencies of
//  its 11 materials cannot resolve from a loaded fastfile. They ship raw here
//  (extracted from zm_nuked.ff with Unlinker --image-format IWI) and are
//  declared by name; pack_iwd.ps1 copies zone_assets\images into mod.iwd's
//  images\ for the runtime pixels. The one shared name,
//  c_gen_arm_rim_mask_norim_c, is NOT declared - it already resolves from the
//  donor, and re-declaring it would only risk stomping it.
//
//  THE MATERIALS POINT AT THE *_dlc5 TECHSETS, which this zone now builds
//  FROM RAW (see below); their pimp_technique_* sub-assets and shader
//  binaries ship in zone_assets	echniques and zone_assets\shader_bin.
//
//  ?? DO NOT ADD THE BURIED/ORIGINS FAMILIES. The gun is gated off on those
//  two maps (zapgun.gsc/zapgun.csc), their actor clientfield budgets are full
//  (32/32 and 31/32), and their zombie materials already live in mod.ff.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
//  THE SWELL IS A VERTEX SHADER (v2.15.49) - the route Treyarch used on Moon.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  User, 2026-09-13: the pre-scaled model steps "look like stop motion... the
//  body swells up, they don't just get larger overall." BO1's
//  pimp_shader_sw4_3d_char_cloth_bloat vertex shader does exactly one thing
//  more than the plain one: after the world transform it adds
//      worldPos += worldNormal * scriptVector3.x
//  and the client ramps scriptVector3.x from 0 to 4.0 over 2.5 s. Every
//  vertex moves out along its own normal, so the body inflates in place.
//
//  DLC5's T6 port never carried that over: its two zombie techsets embed the
//  RETAIL vertex shader (measured 2026-09-12, byte-identical DXBC, no
//  scriptVector in the constant tables), which is why the shader ramp did
//  nothing here and the model-swap detour was built. This build compiles the
//  two techsets FROM RAW (zone_assets\techsets, \techniques, \shader_bin):
//  every technique is DLC5's own, renamed *_zqswell, with the three vertex
//  shaders replaced by ours (zone_source\swell_shader_src, built with fxc):
//    pimp_shader_sw4_3d_char_cloth_53938792_zqswell   lit           (+bloat)
//    pimp_shader_sw4_3d_char_cloth_c4eff3ec_zqswell   lit + shadow  (+bloat)
//    pimp_shader_transformonly_d4f4e04b_zqswell       depth/shadowmap (+bloat,
//                                                     reads NORMAL so the
//                                                     shadow inflates too)
//  The HLSL reproduces retail's DXBC instruction for instruction (constant
//  buffer layouts copied from the retail reflection with packoffset), so the
//  only difference the GPU sees is the one mad on scriptVector3. The 44 pixel
//  shaders are DLC5's bytes, unchanged. The Linker (v0.32 and v0.33 agree,
//  identical output) reflects scriptVector3 out of the DXBC and emits it as a
//  code vertex constant, which is what mapshaderconstant()/setshaderconstant()
//  write at runtime (stock uses the same path for the zombie eye glow).
//  v2.15.51: that mad became SwellOffset() (t6_consts.hlsli), the same push
//  weighted by distance from the stomach in model space - scriptVector3.w is
//  the J_SpineLower height the client ramp sends - so the belly leads and the
//  limbs and head no longer inflate into each other. Same techsets, techniques
//  and constant; only the five vertex shader binaries changed.
//
//  zone_source\zomswell_donor (the DLC5 binary copy) is no longer --load'ed:
//  raw beats a loaded zone, but keeping both would invite a stale copy.
//  The 53 MaximumSwell materials below keep pointing at these techsets.
//  🛑 v2.16.1 - NO HEAD LAYER GOES THROUGH A SWELL SHADER ANY MORE.
//  User, 2026-09-14: *"the zombies heads are disappearing ... don't destroy
//  their heads"*. The eye techset below is built from retail
//  pimp_shader_radiant_190f4788 / unlit_cheap_zombie_eyes_6a8c6a7c, and those
//  two retail shaders take POSITION + COLOR + TEXCOORD and NO NORMAL - the
//  swell rebuild had to ADD a NORMAL0 input to feed SwellOffset. A vertex
//  shader that reads an input the head's own vertex buffer never binds is the
//  one thing here that can make a draw vanish outright, which is exactly the
//  symptom.
//
//  🌟 AND IT BOUGHT NOTHING. It was added in v2.15.46, when the swell was a
//  uniform push and the head had to inflate with the body to stay attached.
//  Since v2.15.51 the swell is a torso ball whose weight is ZERO outside an
//  ellipsoid 30x30x22 around J_SpineLower - a head sits far outside that, so
//  SwellOffset already returns 0 for every head vertex. Running the head
//  through a modified shader to compute zero was pure risk.
//  So: the eye techset is gone, and every head material (lit, _unlit, _u, _ub)
//  is off this list and loads its retail definition from the map's own zone.
//  Heads now render exactly as retail while the body swells. Do not re-add
//  them without first proving the head's vertex decl actually binds a normal.
techniqueset,mc_sw4_3d_char_cloth_4z8fq5wu_dlc5
techniqueset,mc_sw4_3d_char_skin_j92387z3_dlc5

//  ?? THE BLOOD IS RED AGAIN (2026-09-12). User: "the color of what the
//  zombie spews out of its mouth is white for some reason it should be red".
//  Cause: the wavegun donor copied the fx' material names into mod.ff as bare
//  REFERENCES ("material, ,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodburst"). mod.ff resolves first at
//  runtime, and a data-less reference wins the name lookup, so the fx drew with
//  no material (white). Declaring the five names forces the Linker to take the
//  real definitions out of common_zm.ff, which owns all five and loads on every
//  map - the exact assets Treyarch's own blood fx use.
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodburst
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodburst_b_ds64
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodburst_c_ds64
material,gfx_fxt_bio_blooddrops_ds64
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodgush_ds64
//  v2.15.49: the SAME defect, three more names. fx_sizzle_blood_eyes and
//  fx_sizzle_mist also reference these, and the wavegun donor carried them as
//  data-less references too; mod_base.zone no longer lists them, so these
//  declarations pull common_zm's real assets. Moon's eye-blood fx drew as a
//  white sparkle stream while its particle-cloud material had no data.
material,gfx_fxt_env_dust_mote_pcloud_blend
material,gfx_fxt_smk_gen_z10
xmodel,fx_axis_createfx
//  ...and the image behind gfx_fxt_light_hot_add (the beam's hot glow), which
//  the donor inventory also carried data-less. common_zm owns it.
image,fxt_light_hot
