// ============================================================================
//  THE WELDED SWELL COPIES (v2.17.46) - the Der Riese build 11 route.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  User, 2026-09-26: a friend's Wave Gun for Zombies Declassified's Der Riese
//  bloats zombies properly; make ours do the same, as close to Moon as can be.
//  Measured in that build (modding-jobs\wavegun-build11-001): Moon's one-line
//  shader, and at the kill the corpse is swapped to a copy of its body and head
//  whose vertex normals are WELDED - every vertex that shares a position gets
//  the average normal. On a stock mesh the hard edges carry split normals, so a
//  push along the normal tears the surface open there; welded, it inflates as
//  one skin. That tear is why v2.15.51 retreated to a stomach-only ball.
//
//  63 models (every body and head the four maps' basic aitypes spawn, plus the
//  Jumping Jack), all LODs, generated by gen_swell_models.py from the maps' own
//  zones: positions, UVs, weights and skeleton untouched, normals welded.
//  EVERY surface has its own zqwg_ material, so no copy depends on a stock name
//  and none of these can ever collide with a map zone's asset. Lit body/head
//  surfaces run the swell techsets; eye layers and gore keep their stock
//  techsets. zapgun.gsc precaches only the current map's set (16 at most).
// ============================================================================
material,mc/zqwg_mtl_c_zom_brutus_alpha_punch
material,mc/zqwg_mtl_c_zom_chinese_zombie_head1
material,mc/zqwg_mtl_c_zom_chinese_zombie_head1_u
material,mc/zqwg_mtl_c_zom_chinese_zombie_head2
